[
    {
        "content": "<p>It seems that recent instance-removing updates have made <code>ENat</code> more of a pain to work with. <code>norm_num</code> now fails for simple goals involving literals, and <code>rw</code> fails in places where it didn't used to. Here are a couple of examples : </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ENat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">norm_num</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"bp\">∞</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">min</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">min_eq_left</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- exact? gives</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- exact Std.LawfulOrderLeftLeaningMin.min_eq_left a b hab</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- exact min_eq_left hab -- succeeds</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 578399410,
        "sender_full_name": "Peter Nelson",
        "timestamp": 1773150339
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>note that the above issue doesn't occur with <code>backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false</code> and <code>import Mathlib</code></p>",
        "id": 578403271,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1773151116
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>#defeq_abuse in</code> claims the  issue is <code>ℕ∞ =?= WithTop ℕ</code></p>",
        "id": 578403689,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1773151203
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So what is the recommended fix in, say, a PR that wants that kind of rewrite?</p>",
        "id": 578405113,
        "sender_full_name": "Peter Nelson",
        "timestamp": 1773151475
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Probably <code>set backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false</code> at the top of the file, or <code>set backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false in</code> per theorem.<br>\nKim said PRs can turn that flag off wherever they want for the time being</p>",
        "id": 578405392,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1773151537
